  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Initial release of the PublicFunction.DataBase library.\n\n      ✨ Key Features in this version:\n      - **Microsoft SQL Server**: Provides a robust `SQLService` for executing stored procedures and commands with parameter management.\n      - **Redis**: Includes a `RedisManager` for key-value operations, hashes, lists, and sets using StackExchange.Redis.\n      - **MongoDB**: (To be documented) Infrastructure for MongoDB interactions.\n      - **MySQL**: (To be documented) Infrastructure for MySQL database interactions.\n      - **Oracle**: (To be documented) Infrastructure for Oracle database interactions.\n      - **RabbitMQ**: (To be documented) Infrastructure for RabbitMQ message queuing.\n\n      📦 How to use:\n      Each database type has a dedicated manager or service. For example, use `SQLService` for SQL databases and `RedisManager` for Redis cache operations.\n\n      📚 Complete documentation and usage examples are available in the project repository:\n      https://github.com/rayanabniro/PublicFunction/tree/main/PublicFunction.DataBase",
